m but at  the end of the day you have to feel  comfortable with it you have to feel  comfortable either with like if she  sticks to her guns and she's saying  that's all I'm gonna give you then  you're gonna end up with 5% of the  business you either have to feel  comfortable with having that 5% and  growing and building this hopefully  successful company and not having to eat  at you that your own  earning 5% that's dangerous if you're  gonna build this highly successful  company think about yourself five years  down the road you put all this work in  and you only have 5% of the business is  that gonna eat at you every day because  if it is you can't take that deal on the  flip side you have to be willing to walk  away for any type of deal you have to be  willing to walk away at some point  what is that percentage where you walk  away there's a five percent is a 10  percent is a 20 percent you have to have  a number in your head that you feel  comfortable with and stick to your guns  she's really important to this deal but  hey so are you right you can let people  beat you down if you feel you have a lot  of value and you deserve more than five  percent then you fight for it and you'd  be willing to walk away this is not just  for business partnerships this is for  customers this is for employees is for  every negotiation you have you have to  be willing to walk away at some point  when I work with customers and I'll  quote them on something it's usually way  higher than they expect and I'm willing  to walk away because I know they're  getting huge value even though it's way  more expensive than what they thought it  would be way more expensive than what my  competitors might charge I'm bringing  way more value than anybody else and I  believe in that price and if they pay it  I'm happy to do work and they'll feel  good about myself and I'll feel great  about the work that I'm doing and if  they don't pay it then I'll walk away  and I'm happy and I know that I've  